    "title": "Dolphins and Broncos updated list of 2026 NFL draft picks after Jaylen Waddle trade",
    "text": "Dolphins and Broncos updated list of 2026 NFL draft picks after Jaylen Waddle trade originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.The Denver Broncos and Miami Dolphins have pulled off a huge trade involving star wide receiver Jaylen Waddle.AdvertisementAccording to NFL Network's Tom Pelissero, the Broncos are acquiring Waddle and a fourth-round pick from the Dolphins and are sending first-, third- and fourth-round picks to Miami.All of the picks involved in this blockbuster trade are 2026 selections and were the Broncos' and Dolphins' original picks, Pelissero adds.Waddle has long been the subject of trade rumors but the belief was that Miami would need a huge package to actually move him. We would say the Broncos' package qualified as such.Now, the Dolphins are armed with more picks to help their rebuild, and the Broncos get the impact wide receiver they needed alongside Courtland Sutton.AdvertisementHere's where things stand in terms of draft capital for both teams in 2026.The Broncos now have seven picks in the 2026 NFL draft, including two comp selections in the seventh round.Round 2Round 4 (via NO)Round 4 (via MIA)Round 5Round 7Round 7 (projected comp pick)Round 7 (projected comp pick)The fourth-round pick from the New Orleans Saints landed in Denver via the Devaughn Vele trade.Dolphins 2026 NFL draft picksThe Dolphins added two picks to their stable after sending one selection back to the Broncos. Nevertheless, the Broncos are now equipped with 11 selections, including two in the first round.Round 1Round 1 (via DEN)Round 2Round 3Round 3 (via DEN)Round 3 (via PHI)Round 3 (via HOU)Round 4 (via DEN)Round 5Round 7Round 7 (via LAC)The third-round pick from the Philadelphia Eagles came via the Jaelan Phillips trade last season. Miami acquired the third-round pick from the Houston Texans following a 2025 draft-day trade.AdvertisementThe seventh-rounder from the Los Angeles Chargers was acquired in the Minkah Fitzpatrick trade with the New York Jets.More NFL News",
